{
  "name": "Upload an image to Ampost and post it to social media",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Upload an image and post it\n### How it works\nAny binary file in n8n (a download, an email attachment, a Google Drive file) can go into a post: **Upload to Ampost** uploads it and waits until Ampost has checked it, then **Create post** attaches it.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-ampost** (tested with 0.1.1): Settings → Community nodes → Install, as in the [n8n guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/). Until n8n verifies it, the node needs self-hosted n8n.\n2. Create an Ampost credential with an API key from [ampost.io](https://ampost.io/?ref=n8n) → Setup → API keys.\n3. Replace **Download the image** with your file source, and pick the platforms in **Create post**.\n4. Click **Test workflow**.\n\nAccepted: JPEG, PNG, WebP, MP4, MOV and WebM.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "ebdb6572-1f6d-4e45-a5d6-22318c525b33",
      "name": "About this workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "04d702ac-3649-4c6f-aa8c-8c8a555d11a1",
      "name": "Run it",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
